PROP2 - Manual installation on QuickySitter 1.28
=================================================

This kit upgrades the prop system of a QuickySitter 1.28 furniture to
the PROP2 engine. It is OPTIONAL and installed by hand - your furniture
keeps working unchanged if you never install it.

What you gain:
- up to 1024 props per furniture (instead of 100)
- props can no longer be orphaned or removed by other furniture that
  happens to share a chat channel
- leftover attach props clean themselves up
- prop resizing and worn-fit saving without a companion script
- a migration helper that rezzes all your props in one command

Kit contents:
  [QS]prop2       - furniture script, replaces [QS]prop
  [QS]object      - prop script, replaces [AV]object + [QS]objectadjust
  [QS]propRezzer  - migration helper, temporary
  QuickyHUD       - HUD object variant carrying [QS]object
  (this notecard)

You need: modify rights on the furniture, and your prop objects must be
COPY. Make a backup copy of the furniture before you start.


PART A - furniture script
-------------------------
1. Edit the furniture, open the prim inventory that holds the
   [QS] scripts.
2. DELETE [QS]prop.
3. Drop in [QS]prop2.
   Never leave both installed - each would rez every prop twice.
4. Also drop in [QS]propRezzer for the duration of the migration.

Nothing else changes. Your AVpos notecard stays as it is, and the
furniture now runs exactly as before ("mixed state"): existing props
with the old scripts keep working.


PART B - prop objects
---------------------
Every prop object gets the new script. The helper does the tedious
part:

1. Say:  /5 proprezzall
   Every prop object from the furniture inventory rezzes ONCE on a
   grid above the furniture, sleeping (they will not attach or react).
   The chat manifest names each object with its type and grid slot.
   Tip: Ctrl+Alt+T in the viewer highlights invisible objects.
   Use  /5 proprezzall 2  for a wider grid (2 m spacing).
2. For each rezzed copy:
   a. Edit it, open its content tab.
   b. DELETE [AV]object and, if present, [QS]objectadjust.
   c. Drop in [QS]object.
   d. Take the copy back into your inventory.
   e. In the furniture prim inventory, delete the old prop object and
      drop in your edited copy. THE NAME MUST STAY EXACTLY THE SAME,
      otherwise the AVpos PROP lines will not find it.
3. Leftover grid copies: say  /5 propclean
   They are returned to your Lost and Found (needs object return
   rights on the parcel - on foreign land, pick them up by hand).
4. Replace the QuickyHUD object in the furniture inventory with the
   QuickyHUD from this kit (same rule: delete old, drop in new).
5. DELETE [QS]propRezzer from the furniture.

You can migrate props in batches. Migrated and unmigrated props work
side by side as long as you do NOT do Part C.


PART C - the wire switch (optional, only when Part B is COMPLETE)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
The switch raises the prop limit to 1024 and hardens the rez channel.
It requires that EVERY prop object carries [QS]object - an old
[AV]object prop rezzed under the new wire lies inert and must be
deleted by hand.

1. Open the AVpos notecard.
2. Add this line ABOVE the first PROP line:

   PROP2 ON

3. Save. The furniture re-reads the notecard.
4. Sit and click through your poses once. If any prop still carries
   the old script, the furniture names it in chat within ten seconds:
   "... did not answer the v2 handshake ...". Migrate that object
   (Part B) and re-test.

To go back at any time: remove the PROP2 ON line and save.


Verification checklist
----------------------
- pose with a world prop: prop appears, disappears on pose change
- pose with an attach prop: prop attaches (a permission dialog is
  normal on land without the QuickyProducts experience)
- stand up: worn props detach and vanish
- owner-click a rezzed world prop: the size menu opens
- no "did not answer the v2 handshake" warnings (Part C only)

Trouble? All QS scripts announce their version in chat. This kit is
version 1.28 - a furniture on an older QuickySitter must be updated
first.
